      "source": [
        "# Hypothesis Testing\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Hypothesis Definition\n",
        "\n",
        "This section aims to investigate whether productivity exhibits a statistically meaningful linear association with caffeine intake and total sleep duration. \n",
        "\n",
        "- **Null Hypothesis (H₀):** There is no significant relationship between my productivity and my daily caffeine consumption or sleep pattern. \n",
        "- **Alternative Hypothesis (H₁):** There is a significant relationship between my productivity and my daily caffeine consumption or sleep pattern. \n",
        "\n",
        "The hypotheses will be evaluated through Pearson correlation analysis, focusing on caffeine consumption and sleep duration. Evidence of statistically significant associations may lay the groundwork for developing machine learning models that predict productivity using behavioral patterns.\n",
      ]
    },
    {
